smart-object-select bundles model files derived from the following third-party model.

Model: FastSAM-s
Source: https://huggingface.co/anakhiu/fastsam-onnx (`fastsam_s.onnx`)
  (fp32 ONNX export of FastSAM-s / YOLOv8s-seg, ~11.8M params, exported with
  `ultralytics` 8.4.107 at `imgsz=1024`, `opset=17`, simplified with `onnxslim`;
  unmodified — republished verbatim into public/models/fast-sam/ so that
  smart-object-select can serve the model from its own origin instead of fetching
  it from the Hugging Face Hub at runtime)
Original model: https://github.com/CASIA-IVA-Lab/FastSAM (FastSAM-s, class-agnostic
  "segment everything" instance segmentation trained on a subset of SA-1B, built on
  the Ultralytics YOLOv8-seg architecture/training code)

License:
  The upstream CASIA-IVA-Lab/FastSAM repository's own LICENSE file
  (https://github.com/CASIA-IVA-Lab/FastSAM/blob/main/LICENSE) is the full text of
  the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0), even though that repo's
  README.md states "The model is licensed under the Apache 2.0 license" (a
  discrepancy within the upstream repo itself: README claims Apache-2.0, the actual
  LICENSE file is AGPL-3.0). The Hugging Face export used here
  (anakhiu/fastsam-onnx) also declares `license: apache-2.0` in its repository card,
  which is presumed to simply carry over the same upstream README claim rather than
  an independent licensing decision. Given this contradiction, and consistent with
  issue #50 (parent #45) guidance to treat FastSAM the same as YOLO11n-seg
  (public/models/yolo11n-seg/NOTICE) since both are Ultralytics-YOLOv8-seg-derived,
  this file is conservatively licensed and distributed here under AGPL-3.0 (the
  license actually present in the upstream LICENSE file). A copy of the AGPL-3.0
  license text is included at the repository root (`LICENSE`); this repository
  (this smart-object-select project) is published as AGPL-3.0 in full to satisfy
  this requirement (source-available on GitHub, including when accessed over a
  network, per AGPL-3.0 Section 13). This decision follows the same reasoning
  already confirmed with the repository owner for YOLO11n-seg (issue #45 Decision
  Log #4, issue #49).

  Like YOLO11n-seg (AGPL-3.0, public/models/yolo11n-seg/NOTICE) and unlike MobileSAM
  (Apache-2.0, public/models/mobile-sam/NOTICE) / EdgeSAM (S-Lab License 1.0 /
